Package: duckdf
Type: Package
Title: SQL for Dataframes, but with Ducks
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Phill", "Clarke", email = "phill@mimosadev.org",
    role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: An SQL interface for R dataframes built on the DuckDB embedded
    analytical database. Dataframes are registered directly with an in-process
    DuckDB instance and queried with standard SQL, so analyses can join,
    filter, aggregate and reshape R objects with SQL while results are
    returned as dataframes, without copying data to an external database
    server. The package wraps the 'duckdb' R package with a DBI-compliant
    connection and provides a small, checked surface for the common
    register-query-unregister workflow. The underlying engine and its
    vectorised execution model are described in Raasveldt and Mühleisen
    (2019) <doi:10.1145/3299869.3320212>.
